WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.694
Most image converters online want you to upload

2
00:00:02.752 --> 00:00:04.737
your photos to their server first.

3
00:00:05.248 --> 00:00:07.790
This one never does. Everything happens right

4
00:00:07.837 --> 00:00:10.588
here in your browser. Drop in as many images

5
00:00:10.635 --> 00:00:12.597
as you like — there is no file limit

6
00:00:12.666 --> 00:00:15.801
and no queue. Now choose your output format.

7
00:00:16.079 --> 00:00:18.053
PNG keeps transparency,

8
00:00:18.262 --> 00:00:20.189
JPEG is best for photographs,

9
00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:22.744
and WebP is usually the smallest thing you

10
00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:25.692
can put on a website. For the lossy formats

11
00:00:25.809 --> 00:00:27.283
you get a quality slider.

12
00:00:28.096 --> 00:00:30.128
Eighty-two is a sensible default.

13
00:00:30.406 --> 00:00:32.589
Drag it down and the files get smaller.

14
00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:36.014
You can resize too — set a maximum width,

15
00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:38.580
and every image is scaled to fit while keeping

16
00:00:38.626 --> 00:00:41.970
its aspect ratio. Nothing is ever enlarged.

17
00:00:42.214 --> 00:00:45.059
Watch the results. Each row shows the original

18
00:00:45.128 --> 00:00:47.787
size, the new size and exactly how much you

19
00:00:47.857 --> 00:00:50.190
saved. Download one file,

20
00:00:50.306 --> 00:00:51.862
or download the whole batch.

21
00:00:52.559 --> 00:00:54.776
Nothing was uploaded, and the location data

22
00:00:54.834 --> 00:00:56.425
in your photos is gone.
